{#- Default values applied on top of anything set in pillar.

   ssh_agent_autostart is off by default: auto-starting an ssh-agent and
   running ssh-add from .bashrc means a passphrase prompt (or an ssh-add
   error, for accounts with no key) on every new interactive shell. Fine
   for a personal workstation account, surprising for a skel applied
   fleet-wide -- so it's opt-in per pillar rather than on by default.

   use_default/custom_source/includes control /etc/skel/.bashrc's
   content -- see README for the full explanation. Short version:
   use_default (default True) includes this formula's built-in body;
   custom_source (a salt:// path), if set, replaces it; includes is an
   ordered list of extra paths to conditionally source afterward (e.g.
   '$HOME/.bashrc_local' so each user can layer in their own tweaks). #}
{%- set skel_defaults = {
    'enabled': True,
    'mode': '0644',
    'editor': 'nano',
    'ssh_agent_autostart': False,
    'use_default': True,
    'custom_source': '',
    'includes': [],
} %}

{%- set skel = skel_defaults.copy() %}
{%- do skel.update(pillar.get('skel', {})) %}
